==Ice road==
Great Slave Lake has one [[ice road]] known as the Dettah ice road. It is a {{cvt|6.5|km}} road that connects the Northwest Territories capital of Yellowknife to [[Dettah]], a small First Nations fishing community also in the Northwest Territories. To reach the community in summer the drive is {{cvt|27|km}} via the [[Ingraham Trail]].

[[File:Late April on Yellowknife Bay, NWT, Canada..JPG|thumb|center|upright=4|Yellowknife Bay in April 2012. The [[Premelting|surface melt]] begins to make transportation more difficult between the [[houseboat]]s near Jolliffe Island.]]

==In popular culture==
===Television===
From 2014 to 2016, [[Animal Planet]] aired a documentary series called ''[[Ice Lake Rebels]]''. It takes place on Great Slave Lake, and details the lives of houseboaters on the lake.<ref name="Animal Planet (Ice Lake Rebels)">{{cite web | url=http://www.animalplanet.com/tv-shows/ice-lake-rebels/ | title=Ice Lake Rebels | access-date=23 September 2015}}</ref>

[[Alone season 6|Seasons 6]] and [[Alone season 7|7]] of the survival game show ''[[Alone (TV series)|Alone]]'' were set along the shore of the east arm of Great Slave Lake in the [[subarctic]], about {{cvt|250|mi|order=flip}} south of the [[Arctic Circle]] and about {{cvt|70|mi|order=flip}} south of the [[Tree line#Arctic|tree line]]. It follows the self-documented daily struggles of 10 individuals as they survive alone in the [[wilderness]] for as long as possible using a limited amount of [[Survivalism|survival equipment]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=Alone Season 6: Exploring All Filming Locations of the TV Show |url=https://thecinemaholic.com/alone-s06-filming-locations/ |access-date=8 August 2025 |website=www.thecinemaholic.com |first1=Diksha |last1=Sundriyal |date=5 August 2022}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Alone Season 7: Where Are The Contestants Now? |url=https://thecinemaholic.com/alone-season-7-where-are-they-now-2/ |access-date=8 August 2025 |website=www.thecinemaholic.com |first1=Kumari |last1=Shreya |date=2 August 2023}}</ref>

